Comrade Akshat Tripathi, SFI UP State Committee member and a student at Gautam Buddha University, Greater Noida, has been issued a notice by the Greater Noida Executive Magistrate under 130 BNSS acting on a report filed by the UP Police for participating in the ongoing protest at Jantar Mantar and has been ordered to submit a bond of ₹5 lakh under sections related to 'breach of peace.'

Comrade Akshat had participated in a peaceful protest at Jantar Mantar, where a large number of students and youth were demanding accountability from the government and the Education Minister regarding paper leaks, unemployment, and the crumbling education system. This mass movement received support from students and youth across India; during the protest, Comrade Akshat sustained serious injuries on 20th July in the peaceful march to the Parliament when the Delhi police resorted brutality.

The UP Police under the double-engine BJP-RSS government has accused comrade Akshat of inciting and provoking students against the government during the Jantar Mantar protest, while for the past three months Gautam Buddha University remains closed. At the same time, during the Jantar Mantar protest, gundas like Swatantra Bharadwaj safeguarded by the BJP,  Sangh Pariwar and the police were sent to assault peaceful protestors and derail a peaceful protest of the masses.

This order against Akshat comes despite a clear ruling by the Hon'ble Supreme Court stating that no legal action would be taken against any protester involved in the Jantar Mantar movement. Yet, the Uttar Pradesh government and police are making a mockery of the Supreme Court's orders.

The Students' Federation of India (SFI) strongly condemns this repressive action by the Uttar Pradesh government and police. The SFI demands an immediate halt to the BJP government's practice of using the police apparatus to intimidate and suppress democratic voices, and calls for the immediate withdrawal of the order issued against Comrade Akshat.

